#: Part2_Protonation.md:25
msgid ""
"These energetic contributions can impact significantly thermodynamic "
"equilibria, change conformational probabilities and balance between "
"populations. Therefore, using these relationships, we will see how we are "
"able to plot titration curves, estimate pKa values and measure energy "
"differences using CpH-metaD simulations."
msgstr ""
"このエネルギーは熱力学的平衡、Conformation の確率、Population の釣り合いに大きく影響します。これらの関係を使い、CpH-"
"MetaD から Titration Curve、pKa、エネルギー差を求めます。"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:27
msgid ""
"In the uridine system, the nucleobase has a pKa of 9.22 at the N3 atom. This"
" means that at pH < pKa, most of the population should be protonated, hence "
"in a neutral state. While for pH > pKa, most of the population should be "
"deprotonated, hence in a negatively charged state. How do these charge "
"variations impact our system? Can we measure changes in protonation at "
"different pH values and along the simulation time? Is each energy minima "
"distinguishable by their average protonation? If so, then why and how does "
"electrostatics play a role?"
msgstr ""
"Uridine の N3 の pKa は9.22です。pH < pKa では多くが Protonated で中性、pH > pKa では "
"Deprotonated で負電荷を持つはずです。電荷変化は系にどう影響しますか？pH や時間による Protonation "
"変化を測れますか？各極小は平均 Protonation で区別できますか？その理由と静電相互作用の役割は何ですか？"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:29
msgid "These are all questions to be addressed in the following section."
msgstr "次の節でこれらを調べます。"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:31
msgid "Extracting the protonation data"
msgstr "Protonation データの抽出"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:33
msgid ""
"We need to extract the protonation data stored in the .occ files. These "
"files contain information of the proton occupation state of each titrable "
"site along segments of the simulation. These files are generated after each "
"cycle of CpHMD and the total number of lines matches the $ "
"Time_{seg}/\\tau_{p} $, which is the time of segment (1000 ps) over the "
"frequency of protonation (20 ps)."
msgstr ""
".occ から Protonation データを抽出します。各 Segment の各 Titration Site の Proton "
"Occupation State が保存されています。CpHMD の各 Cycle 後に生成され、行数は $ Time_{seg}/\\tau_{p} "
"$、すなわち Segment 時間（1000 ps）を Protonation 間隔（20 ps）で割った数です。"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:35
msgid ""
"Each column corresponds to a distinct titrable site and each row to "
"different timestamps (typically every 20 ps). Then the occupation state is "
"defined by the parametrized states found in the St-XOL3_DelPHi folder. For "
"example, the uridine has two states: URN0 and URN1. URN0 refers to the "
"neutral (0) state, hence the protonated state, while URN1 refers to the "
"charged (-1) state, hence the deprotonated state. In the .occ file, if the "
"occupation state is 0, then it means it is protonated. However, for the "
"adenine, the AR0 also refers to the neutral state, however in this case it "
"is the deprotonated state, and AR1 is the protonated (+1) state. Hence in "
"this specific case, the protonation and occupation states match and we don't"
" need to correct. Typically, binary protonable sites do not need to be "
"corrected, as for the adenine and cytidine, while deprotonable sites "
"(uridine and guanine) require this conversion to obtain the protonation "
"states. Sites with multiple tautomers always need a correction since in "
"those cases, each occupation state refers to a different position of the "
"proton."
msgstr ""
"各列は Titration Site、各行は時刻（通常20 ps ごと）です。Occupation State は St-XOL3_DelPHi "
"のパラメータ化した状態で定義します。Uridine の URN0 は中性 (0) で Protonated、URN1 は荷電 (-1) で "
"Deprotonated なので、.occ の0は Protonated を意味します。一方 Adenine の AR0 は中性ですが "
"Deprotonated、AR1 は Protonated (+1) なので、Occupation と Protonation "
"が一致し補正不要です。通常、二値の Protonable Site（Adenine、Cytidine）は補正不要で、Deprotonable "
"Site（Uridine、Guanine）は変換が必要です。複数 Tautomer では、Occupation が異なる Proton "
"位置を表すため常に補正します。"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:38
msgid ""
"First, we are going to generate a data frame to store all the data found in "
"the .occ files for the different pH values."
msgstr "まず各 pH の .occ を格納する DataFrame を作ります。"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:79
msgid ""
"After extracting all the data and assigning the proper timestamps, we can "
"define the frequency of protonation. While we only calculate the protonation"
" information every 20~ps, in reality, we can propagate the stored "
"protonation states to the intermediate frames within each protonation "
"calculation. If the simulation timestep is 2 ps and the $\\tau_{p}$ is 20 "
"ps, then the protonation states of these intermediate frames correspond to "
"the state assigned in the previous cycle."
msgstr ""
"全データを抽出して時刻を割り当てた後、Protonation の頻度を定義します。計算は20 ps ごとですが、中間 Frame "
"にも状態を割り当てられます。シミュレーションの刻みが2 ps、$\\tau_{p}$ が20 ps なら、中間 Frame は前の Cycle "
"の状態です。"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:105
msgid ""
"Since we are performing CpH-Metadynamics simulations, we require the weight "
"data from the accumulated bias in the simulation. Protonation and "
"conformation are intrinsically coupled, then biased conformations dictate "
"that their protonation states should also be unbiased. To do that we need to"
" obtain the weights and correctly assign them to the corresponding frames."
msgstr ""
"CpH-Metadynamics なので、蓄積 Bias の重みが必要です。Protonation と Conformation "
"は本質的に結合しているため、Conformation だけでなく Protonation State の Bias も除きます。重みを取得し、正しい "
"Frame に割り当てます。"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:142
msgid ""
"Q8. Examine the final dataframe. Do the timestamps of the protonation states"
" match the conformational data? Are all the pH values present?"
msgstr ""
"Q8. 最終 DataFrame で、Protonation の時刻は Conformation と一致しますか？全 pH が含まれていますか？"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:144
msgid ""
"After obtaining the final dataframe with all the pH values, protonation and "
"conformation data and the weights, we can calculate average protonations, "
"derive a titration curve, and estimate the pKa. To plot a titration curve, "
"we need to redefine the Henderson-Hasselbalch (HH) relationship between pH, "
"pKa and protonation. We can rewrite the HH function as follows:"
msgstr ""
"全 pH、Protonation、Conformation、重みを含む DataFrame から、平均 Protonation、Titration "
"Curve、pKa を求められます。曲線用に Henderson-Hasselbalch (HH) の pH・pKa・Protonation "
"関係を書き換えます。"

#: Part2_Protonation.md:148
msgid ""
"where <P> is the average protonation at a certain pH value, pH is the "
"assigned value of the simulation and the pKa is the fitted parameter. "
"However, we are dealing with biased simulations, then we need to calculate "
"the weighted average protonations:"
msgstr ""
"<P> は特定 pH での平均 Protonation、pH は実行時の値、pKa は Fit パラメータです。Bias 付きなので Weighted "
"Average Protonation を求めます。"
